# EXTERNAL PATCH — DO NOT apply inside this repo.
#
# Rationale: skill-registry/SKILL.md is an external gentleman-programming skill file
# distributed to both ~/.claude/skills/skill-registry/SKILL.md and
# ~/.config/opencode/skills/skill-registry/SKILL.md (byte-identical copies — apply this patch
# to BOTH). The repo does not own a copy of this file. Two lines make a transient discovery
# failure authoritative:
#   - line 29 "No skills found -> Write an empty registry so agents stop searching blindly"
#     lets an empty/failed scan (fd/eza missing, stdout swallowed by 2>/dev/null) be PERSISTED
#     as an empty registry — turning a tool failure into authoritative wrong data.
#   - line 34 "Scan all known user and project skill directories for */SKILL.md" prescribes a
#     bare scan with no portability guard and no fail-loud handling.
#
# Honors REGISTRY-AUTHORITATIVE (never persist "zero" from an unverified scan), PORTABLE
# DISCOVERY (command -v guard + POSIX fallback), and FAIL-LOUD (no bare 2>/dev/null or
# || true; missing tool / unreadable source => visible message + scan marked inconclusive).

--- a/skills/skill-registry/SKILL.md
+++ b/skills/skill-registry/SKILL.md
@@ -23,12 +23,16 @@

 ## Decision Gates

 | Situation | Action |
 | --- | --- |
 | Same skill exists globally and in project | Keep the project-level skill |
 | Same skill exists in multiple global locations | Keep the first source in scan order |
-| No skills found | Write an empty registry so agents stop searching blindly |
+| Scan returned zero AND every source dir was confirmed present and readable | Genuinely empty: write an empty registry |
+| Scan returned zero but a source dir was missing/unreadable, or a discovery tool was absent/errored | INCONCLUSIVE — do NOT overwrite the registry as empty. Preserve any existing registry, emit a visible warning naming the tool/dir/error, and stop. A failed scan is never proof of "zero skills". |
 | Agent will delegate work | Select matching registry rows and pass their `SKILL.md` paths |

 ## Execution Steps

-1. Scan all known user and project skill directories for `*/SKILL.md`.
+1. Scan all known user and project skill directories for `*/SKILL.md` using portable, tool-guarded discovery: guard every discovery command with `command -v <tool>` and fall back to POSIX `find`/`ls`; never assume `fd`/`eza`/`bat` exist. NEVER append a bare `2>/dev/null` or `|| true` to a discovery command — a missing tool or unreadable source dir MUST produce a visible, actionable message and mark the scan INCONCLUSIVE rather than empty (see Decision Gates).
 2. Read frontmatter only as needed to extract `name` and `description` trigger text.
 3. Render `.atl/skill-registry.md` with scanned sources, registry contract, skill name, trigger/description, scope, and exact path.
 4. Persist to Engram when available using `title: skill-registry`, `topic_key: skill-registry`, `type: config`, and `capture_prompt: false`.
 5. Return the registry path, skill count, cache status, and whether Engram was updated.
